{
  "total": 65,
  "totalPage": 2,
  "page": 2,
  "pageSize": 50,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4bc",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 667,
      "bookHadithIndex": 51,
      "text": "Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated from his father:\"I was sitting with the Prophet when a woman came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I gave a slave girl to my mother in charity and she died.' He said: 'Your reward is already established, and your right to inherit her has returned it (that Sadaqah) to you.' She said: 'O Messenger of Allah! There was a month of fasting due on her, shall I perform the fast for her?' He said: 'Fast on her behalf.' She said: 'O Messenger of Allah! She never performed Hajj, shall I perform Hajj for her?' He said: 'Yes, perform Hajj on her behalf",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-667-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-667-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-667-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-667-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4bd",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 668,
      "bookHadithIndex": 52,
      "text": "Ibn Umar narrated that :Umar gave a horse to be used in the cause of Allah. Then he saw it being sold, so he wanted to buy it, but the Prophet said: \"Do not take back what you have given in charity",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-668-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-668-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-668-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-668-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4be",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 669,
      "bookHadithIndex": 53,
      "text": "Ikrimah narrated from Ibn Abbas that :a man said: \"O Messenger of Allah! My mother died, will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf?\" He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I have a Makhraf, so bear witness that I have given it in charity on her behalf",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-669-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-669-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-669-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4bf",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 670,
      "bookHadithIndex": 54,
      "text": "Abu Umamah Al-Bahili said:\"During a sermon of his in the year of the Farewell Hajj, I heard the Messenger of Allah say: 'A woman is not to spend anything from her husbands house without her husband's permission.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What about food?' He said: 'That is our most virtuous wealth",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-670-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-670-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-670-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-670-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4c0",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 671,
      "bookHadithIndex": 55,
      "text": "Aishah narrated that :the Prophet said: \"When a woman gives in charity from her husband's house, she will get the reward for it, and for her husband is the same as that, and for the trustee is the same as that. The reward of each them will not be decreased at all by the reward of the other, for him is what he earned, and for her is what she spent",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-671-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-671-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-671-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4c1",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 672,
      "bookHadithIndex": 56,
      "text": "Aishah narrated that:the Messenger of Allah said: \"When a woman gives from her husband's home, with a good heart, not to spoil it, then she will get a reward similar to his, for her is the good she intended - and the same is for the trustee",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-672-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-672-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-672-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-672-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4c2",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 673,
      "bookHadithIndex": 57,
      "text": "Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated:\"We would give Zakat Al-Fitr - when the Messenger of Allah was among us - as a Sa of food, or a Sa of barely, or a Sa of dried dates, or a Sa of raisins, or a Sa of cheese. So we did not stop paying it (like that) until Mu'awiyah arrived in Al-Madinah and talked (about it). Among the things he addressed the people with, he said: 'I see that two Mudd of the wheat of Ash-Sham are equal to a Sa of dried dates.' So the people followed that.\" Abu Sa'eed said: \"I will not stop giving it in the manner that I had been giving it",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-673-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-673-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-673-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-673-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4c3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 674,
      "bookHadithIndex": 58,
      "text": "Amr bin Shu'aib narrated from his grandfather that :the Prophet sent a caller in the roads of Makkah proclaiming \"Sadaqatul-Fitr is required upon every Muslim, male or female, free or slave, young or old; it is two Mudd of wheat or its equivalent of a Sa of food",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-674-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-674-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-674-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4c4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 675,
      "bookHadithIndex": 59,
      "text": "Ibn Umar narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah made Sadaqatul-Fitr an obligation upon the male and female, the free and the bondsmen, as a Sa of dried dates or a Sa of barley.\" He said: \"So the people equated that to half a Sa of wheat",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-675-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-675-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-675-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-675-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4c5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 676,
      "bookHadithIndex": 60,
      "text": "Ibn Umar narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah made Sadaqatul-Fitr of Ramadan an obligation - a Sa of dried dates or a Sa of barley - required upon every free person and slave, male and female among the Muslims",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-676-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-676-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-676-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-676-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4c6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 677,
      "bookHadithIndex": 61,
      "text": "Ibn Umar narrated that :the Messenger of Allah would order paying the Zakat before going to the Salat on the day of Fitr",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-677-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-677-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-677-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-677-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Agreed Upon"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4c7",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 678,
      "bookHadithIndex": 62,
      "text": "Ali narrated:\"Al-Abbas asked the Messenger of Allah about paying his charity (Zakat) in advance before its time is due (by being in possession for a whole year), he permitted him to do that",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-678-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-678-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-678-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4c8",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 679,
      "bookHadithIndex": 63,
      "text": "Ali narrated that :the Prophet said to Umar: \"We have taken this year's Zakat from Al-Abbas in the previous year",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-679-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-679-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-679-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4c9",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 680,
      "bookHadithIndex": 64,
      "text": "Abu Hurairah narrated that he heard :the Messenger of Allah saying: \"For one of you to go out early to gather firewood and carry it on his back so that he can give charity from it and be free of need from the people, is better for him than to ask a man who may give that to him or refuse. Indeed the upper hand (giving) is more virtuous than the lower hand (receiving), and begin with (those who are) your dependants",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-680-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-680-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-680-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-680-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b4ca",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322",
      "bookIndex": 7,
      "hadithIndex": 681,
      "bookHadithIndex": 65,
      "text": "Samurah bin Jundub narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \"Asking is a labor that toils on a man's face, except if a man asks for something from the Sultan (ruler), or he asks for something that he cannot do without",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-681-ahmadmuhammadshakir",
          "name": "Ahmad Muhammad Shakir",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-681-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-681-basharawadmaarouf",
          "name": "Bashar Awad Maarouf",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-7-681-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}